\name{cellucid_analysis_result}
\alias{cellucid_analysis_result}
\title{Read an analysis result}
\usage{
cellucid_analysis_result(viewer, analysis, in_ = "panel", top = 20)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{analysis}{An analysis with a Run button. One of \code{"markers"}, \code{"differential"}, \code{"dotplot"}, \code{"signature"}, \code{"composition"}, \code{"correlation"}. Required.}
\item{in_}{Either exactly \code{"panel"} (The Analysis panel); or a whole number (at least 1) (A floating analysis window, by its number (1 is the first open)). Default \code{"panel"}, the viewer's own. Sent as the parameter \code{in}.}
\item{top}{At most this many rows: per group of marker genes, per direction of a differential expression (top 40: 40 up in A and 40 up in B); about.rows says how it counted. A whole number (at least 1). Default \code{20}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{about} (How it was computed, as its expanded view's statistics say: the groups and their cells (samples), the test and its pairing (pseudobulk: its limma model), the correction, the expression matrix and its values, the fold change, tests between pages or groups, what the rows are), \code{analysis}, \code{columns}, \code{computed_on} (What the result was computed on), \code{rows}, \code{stale}, \code{stale_reasons}, \code{total_rows} (Rows in the whole result). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The top rows of an analysis's result table (N a parameter), with how it was tested (groups and their cells, test, matrix), what it was computed on and whether it is stale.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{analysis.result} (Analysis). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_analysis_result(viewer, analysis = "markers")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
